Scope of this repository
------------------------
Everything under hybrid_moa_vl_operator_suite/ is byte-identical to the
shipped archive, including the import fixes it carries (if __package__:
dual-mode imports, and the persistent sparse top-k megakernel exposed under
both persistent_moa_norm_sparse_topk_megakernel and
persistent_norm_sparse_topk_agg_kernel in every environment).

The only files written for this repository are smoke_test.py, README.md,
NOTICE, .gitignore, the files under docs/ and the render/verification tooling
under viz/; they are covered by the LICENSE file below.

Upstream defects found and fixed here
-------------------------------------
Four Triton launch sites in the operator package passed argument names that do
not exist in the corresponding @triton.jit kernel signatures, so every GPU
(code path) forward pass raised TypeError. The NumPy path was unaffected, which
is why CPU-only testing never caught them. Fixed here (one line each):

  baryogenesis_parity_operators.py:516
      delta_mass=delta_mass      ->  delta_mass_sq=delta_mass ** 2
  neuro_nonlinear_operators.py:463
      fhn_kappa=fhn_kappa        ->  kappa_sq3=3.0 * (fhn_kappa ** 2)
  quantum_tidal_operators.py:481
      M_HARM=M                    ->  M_HARMONICS=M
  supermembrane_spacetime_operators.py:497
      tau_brane=..., beta_flux=... ->  tau_sq=tau_brane ** 2, beta_sq=beta_flux ** 2

The squared / cubed forms match the NumPy reference implementations in the same
files. viz/check_gpu_launch.py now runs all 14 domain operators forward+backward
on CUDA and cross-checks each against the CPU path, so this class of defect is
caught automatically from now on.

Per-module license headers were deliberately not inserted, so the operator
files stay byte-identical to the shipped archive.

